{"packet_id":"D048-01","doc_id":"D048","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts ban on local rent control (Chapter 40P opt-in exception)","requirement":"No city or town may enact, maintain or enforce rent control, except a city or town that accepts this chapter may adopt rent control regulation, which becomes voluntary for owners after six months and cannot cover evictions or small owners.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All cities and towns in Massachusetts; a city or town that accepts this chapter may adopt rent control regulation subject to the chapter's limits.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Municipal opt-in rent control may not apply to units owned by a person or entity owning fewer than 10 rental units, or to units with fair market rent over $400; owner compliance voluntary after 6 months."},"exemptions":"Municipalities accepting the chapter may regulate rent, but compliance is voluntary and uncoerced after six months; regulation may not cover occupancy, services, evictions, condominium conversion or removal, nor units of owners with fewer than 10 rental units or units with fair market rent over $400.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 40P, § 4","quoted_span":"Section 4. No city or town may enact, maintain or enforce rent control of any kind, except that any city or town that accepts this chapter may adopt rent control regulation that provides:","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D048-01","doc_id":"D048","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts limit on municipal rent control regulating evictions","requirement":"Municipal rent control regulation adopted under this chapter may not include the regulation of occupancy, services, evictions, condominium conversion or the removal of properties from such regulation.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Applies to rent control regulation adopted by a city or town that accepts this chapter; the state itself prohibits rent control generally.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Limits what an accepting municipality's rent control regulation may cover."},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 40P, § 4","quoted_span":"(b) such regulation may not include the regulation of occupancy, services, evictions, condominium conversion or the removal of properties from such regulation,","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
